# Lab 8 rules (do not break these)

- Only beginner Python: variables, if/elif/else, loops, lists, dictionaries, `random`, and text files.
- No classes. No imports besides `random`.
- Never rename or change the parameters of `roll_die`, `log_event`, `fight`, `save_checkpoint`, `load_checkpoint`, or `main`.
- `fight(hero)` must still return `True` or `False`.
- Keep `SAVE_FILE`, `LOG_FILE`, and `STARTING_HP` exactly as they are.
- Menu options 1-4 stay exactly as they are. New features go in option 5 and up.
- After every change, `python check_lab.py` must still show 21/21. If it drops, fix that before adding anything else.
- Explain every line you add or change in plain language, so it can be read aloud to the guild.
- Prefer small, testable steps over big rewrites.
